.TH WAIT_NOHANG 3
.SH NAME
wait_nohang \- wait for a child process without blocking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "wait.h"
.PP
.BI "int wait_nohang(int* " wstat ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wait_nohang
waits for a child process to change state. If no child has changed state,
it returns 0 immediately without blocking. If a child has changed state,
the exit status is stored in
.I wstat
and the process ID of the child is returned.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the PID of the child that changed state, 0 if no child is ready,
or -1 on error.